WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.314
Oh, so this is the color when it’s hot.

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:02.148
That means I’m hot.

00:00:02.915 --> 00:00:04.711
(No, the weather is hot.)

00:00:04.805 --> 00:00:05.617
Auntie just killed it for me.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.610
Hey! That’s a filming set.

00:00:07.739 --> 00:00:09.413
This girl right here is an actress.

00:00:09.973 --> 00:00:11.410
Bonnie Pattraphus.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.484
Can you hear my voice?

00:00:13.444 --> 00:00:14.194
Can you hear me?

00:00:14.903 --> 00:00:15.702
Of course, you can.

00:00:15.737 --> 00:00:16.871
Don’t pretend you can’t.

00:00:17.728 --> 00:00:18.870
- Sawasdee ka.
- Sawasdee ka.

00:00:18.915 --> 00:00:19.985
I’m Emi.

00:00:20.007 --> 00:00:21.130
I’m Bonnie.

00:00:21.314 --> 00:00:22.854
Welcome to Vlog of Us!

00:00:22.865 --> 00:00:24.554
Today, fate will decide where we’re going.

00:00:24.885 --> 00:00:26.865
- We have three options.
- (You can choose only one.)

00:00:26.884 --> 00:00:27.714
I’ll let Bonnie pick.

00:00:27.808 --> 00:00:28.480
Which one will you pick?

00:00:28.819 --> 00:00:29.848
This one!

00:00:30.019 --> 00:00:32.337
Ah, look!

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.176
We got Talat Noi.

00:00:34.194 --> 00:00:36.391
That’s your favorite place, right?

00:00:36.456 --> 00:00:37.299
I go there sometimes.

00:00:37.314 --> 00:00:37.936
What?
[YOU SAID YOU GO THERE A LOT.]

00:00:37.936 --> 00:00:38.850
[YOU SAID YOU GO THERE A LOT.]

00:00:38.894 --> 00:00:40.668
I visit sometimes, but not much lately.

00:00:40.681 --> 00:00:41.527
I kinda forgot about it.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.296
I’ve barely been there at all.

00:00:43.388 --> 00:00:45.684
- Be my tour guide?
- If I can, I will.

00:00:45.788 --> 00:00:47.361
- Let’s go!
- Let’s go!

00:00:47.758 --> 00:00:49.297
So, right now, we’re at…

00:00:49.312 --> 00:00:50.607
Talat Noi!

00:00:51.136 --> 00:00:52.060
Yeah!

00:00:52.146 --> 00:00:53.134
Have you been here before?

00:00:53.222 --> 00:00:54.365
Not this alley.

00:00:54.385 --> 00:00:55.482
I have!

00:00:55.511 --> 00:00:58.290
I shot my first thesis here.
	[SHE CAME HERE FOR HER THESIS.]

00:00:58.322 --> 00:00:59.099
Where are we heading next?

00:00:59.228 --> 00:01:00.823
(You have to pick the next spot.)

00:01:00.842 --> 00:01:02.872
So, we have to choose every time?

00:01:02.998 --> 00:01:03.509
(That’s right.)

00:01:03.533 --> 00:01:05.194
- Yeah?
- Ah, okay.

00:01:05.697 --> 00:01:06.951
Café of Us!

00:01:07.005 --> 00:01:08.065
What are the options?

00:01:08.139 --> 00:01:09.165
We’ve got three choices.

00:01:09.343 --> 00:01:10.694
Is there a matcha café?

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.379
I’d love to hit a cocoa café too.

00:01:12.444 --> 00:01:14.005
Alright. Hope you get it!

00:01:14.188 --> 00:01:15.229
- This one!
- The one in the middle!

00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:18.370
[WILL THEY GET THE SPOT THEY WANT?]

00:01:18.463 --> 00:01:19.970
Nope!
[BOTH FAILED.]

00:01:20.084 --> 00:01:22.948
- What is this place… Vanich House?
- We’ll let fate do the job.

00:01:23.038 --> 00:01:23.635
Have you been there before?

00:01:23.654 --> 00:01:24.327
Nope.

00:01:24.337 --> 00:01:26.875
No? Well, today’s your first time!

00:01:27.302 --> 00:01:29.088
Bonnie, do you know the way to the café?

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:29.811
Not at all.

00:01:29.887 --> 00:01:31.170
The staff said to go this way.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.521
[WILL THESE TWO GET LOST?]

00:01:32.521 --> 00:01:34.145
Let’s check the area out first.
[WILL THESE TWO GET LOST?]

00:01:34.145 --> 00:01:34.499
Come on!
[WILL THESE TWO GET LOST?]

00:01:35.032 --> 00:01:37.179
They have an accessories shop too.

00:01:37.194 --> 00:01:38.401
I love this kind of stuff.

00:01:38.571 --> 00:01:39.394
Wanna check it out? Let’s go.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.887
Wow. A butterfly!

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:43.034
I’ll take this one.

00:01:44.318 --> 00:01:45.632
Does it suit me?

00:01:46.162 --> 00:01:47.973
It looks really cute on you.

00:01:48.202 --> 00:01:49.973
It changes color with temperature?

00:01:49.985 --> 00:01:52.434
(Yes! In an air-conditioned room,)

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:54.834
(it turns pinkish-purple.)

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.050
Oh, so this is the color when it’s hot.

00:01:56.062 --> 00:01:56.902
That means I’m hot.

00:01:57.657 --> 00:01:59.511
(No, the weather is hot.)

00:01:59.527 --> 00:02:01.121
- Can I try it on to see if I’m hot too?
- Ah! Auntie just killed it for me.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.564
[YOU’RE NOT HOT, GIRL. THE WEATHER IS.]

00:02:02.564 --> 00:02:03.531
Auntie, you’re such a vibe killer!
[YOU’RE NOT HOT, GIRL. THE WEATHER IS.]

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.417
- (You look sweet, not the hot type.)
- Aww!

00:02:08.608 --> 00:02:10.214
What about me, Auntie?

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.890
(You’re pretty with a cool vibe.)

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:14.330
[NICE ONE, AUNTIE.]

00:02:14.705 --> 00:02:15.610
Right!

00:02:15.625 --> 00:02:16.453
Auntie, did you make this yourself?

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:20.171
I’ll take the butterfly—our symbol.

00:02:20.386 --> 00:02:23.023
- Bonnie, can you help me put it on?
- Ooh, it’s in black.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:25.404
(It’s a little loose.)

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:26.351
Can you help me with this?

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.294
Of course.

00:02:27.657 --> 00:02:29.109
Tight or loose?

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.160
Loose.

00:02:30.488 --> 00:02:31.400
Or it’ll be right on my double chin.

00:02:33.306 --> 00:02:34.128
How does it look?

00:02:34.291 --> 00:02:34.786
Done!

00:02:34.797 --> 00:02:37.349
Wow! So pretty.

00:02:37.475 --> 00:02:38.752
What do you think, guys?

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:40.591
(It matches Emi’s top today.)

00:02:40.724 --> 00:02:42.025
We’re matching!

00:02:42.025 --> 00:02:43.170
[ACCIDENTALLY MATCHING.]

00:02:43.413 --> 00:02:46.112
After finishing our accessory shopping…

00:02:46.139 --> 00:02:49.367
Right behind us is
a charcoal-grilled bread shop.

00:02:50.094 --> 00:02:51.802
They even have grilled bread
with Chinese sausage!

00:02:51.832 --> 00:02:53.071
I’m not a fan of Chinese sausage.

00:02:53.419 --> 00:02:54.263
That’s fine—I like it.

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:57.297
- Give it a try. You might end up liking it!
- But I do like roasted chili paste.

00:02:57.539 --> 00:02:59.140
All right, I’ll keep an open mind.

00:02:59.774 --> 00:03:00.868
Cheers!

00:03:05.722 --> 00:03:07.797
Mmm, it’s good.

00:03:08.158 --> 00:03:08.685
It really is.

00:03:08.928 --> 00:03:11.014
- Thank you, ma’am!
- The chili paste is top-notch.

00:03:11.053 --> 00:03:12.042
Yeah, it’s really good!

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.586
Right now, we are…

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:17.451
Lost.

00:03:17.451 --> 00:03:17.850
[THEY ARE LOST.]

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:18.642
Where’s the café?
[THEY ARE LOST.]

00:03:18.642 --> 00:03:18.654
[THEY ARE LOST.]

00:03:18.654 --> 00:03:19.050
Look over there.
[THEY ARE LOST.]

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:19.835
Look over there.

00:03:20.051 --> 00:03:21.226
There are lots of people.

00:03:21.336 --> 00:03:22.900
Hey! That’s a filming set.

00:03:23.241 --> 00:03:24.785
Excuse me, can we join you?

00:03:24.808 --> 00:03:26.607
This girl right here is an actress—

00:03:27.152 --> 00:03:28.497
Bonnie Pattraphus.
[ZIP IT.]

00:03:28.497 --> 00:03:29.570
[ZIP IT.]

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.330
[SHE’S HAPPY SHE GETS TO TEASE BONNIE.]

00:03:32.128 --> 00:03:33.103
Hey!

00:03:33.211 --> 00:03:35.007
I’ve never been down this alley before, guys.

00:03:35.037 --> 00:03:36.257
Bonnie, your necklace is stunning.

00:03:37.727 --> 00:03:38.911
It really stands out.

00:03:41.048 --> 00:03:42.250
And your bracelet is so beautiful.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:42.911
[WHEN NO ONE COMPLIMENTS US,
WE COMPLIMENT EACH OTHER.]

00:03:42.911 --> 00:03:44.130
Can the camera see it?
[WHEN NO ONE COMPLIMENTS US,
WE COMPLIMENT EACH OTHER.]

00:03:46.478 --> 00:03:48.155
The café is right in front of us.

00:03:48.202 --> 00:03:48.848
We’re almost there.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:49.321
[WE’RE HERE!]

00:03:49.321 --> 00:03:50.330
Vanich House.
[WE’RE HERE!]

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:51.700
Today, I’m just here to eat, sir.

00:03:51.751 --> 00:03:54.090
Okay. Guys, we made it to Vanich House.

00:03:54.604 --> 00:03:56.256
- Let’s head inside and eat.
- Let’s go!

00:03:56.648 --> 00:03:58.017
What would you like, kiddo?

00:03:58.062 --> 00:03:59.128
They have bagels too.

00:03:59.145 --> 00:04:00.248
What would you like, Bonnie?

00:04:00.785 --> 00:04:01.693
What do you like?

00:04:01.945 --> 00:04:03.722
Everything looks delicious—I can’t decide.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:04.413
Pick something for me.

00:04:04.518 --> 00:04:05.936
Every time I pick for you, you don’t like it.

00:04:06.591 --> 00:04:07.834
Have I ever not liked food?

00:04:07.989 --> 00:04:09.595
You never like what I choose for you.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:10.934
[SOMEONE’S GETTING SULKY.]

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:11.431
Wait.
[SOMEONE’S GETTING SULKY.]

00:04:11.431 --> 00:04:11.454
[SOMEONE’S GETTING SULKY.]

00:04:11.454 --> 00:04:12.210
Really?
[SOMEONE’S GETTING SULKY.]

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:12.222
Really?

00:04:12.447 --> 00:04:13.641
Look, it’s Dokrak! (*Crown Flower)
[CROWN FLOWER EARRINGS.]

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.388
Dokrak earrings—so cute!
[CROWN FLOWER EARRINGS.]

00:04:16.395 --> 00:04:17.050
Aren’t they adorable?

00:04:17.158 --> 00:04:18.247
Seriously, they’re so cute.

00:04:18.277 --> 00:04:19.866
Do you think this is destiny, guys?

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.066
We’re gonna go broke today.

00:04:21.241 --> 00:04:22.804
Yep, completely bankrupt.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:23.962
Hey, I think this one is even prettier.

00:04:23.989 --> 00:04:24.906
Ooh, they have postcards too!

00:04:24.918 --> 00:04:26.402
Bonnie, this set has two.

00:04:27.094 --> 00:04:27.962
Which one do you want?

00:04:28.014 --> 00:04:29.111
Which one’s cuter?

00:04:29.142 --> 00:04:30.517
I think this one is a nice size…

00:04:30.653 --> 00:04:31.545
Is it too big?

00:04:31.666 --> 00:04:33.456
So this one has two flowers,
but this one only has one.

00:04:33.537 --> 00:04:35.977
Just pick whichever you like. I’ll pay.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:39.059
- Really? It’s okay, you don’t have to.
- I mean it. Don’t worry about it.

00:04:39.077 --> 00:04:39.842
No…

00:04:39.857 --> 00:04:40.402
I feel shy.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.743
Why do you always reject me
when I offer to pay?

00:04:41.767 --> 00:04:42.450
I don’t get it.

00:04:42.637 --> 00:04:43.400
Fine, you can pay.

00:04:43.417 --> 00:04:43.980
There you go.

00:04:43.997 --> 00:04:44.602
You choose.

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:46.117
You’re not gonna like what I pick. I just know it.

00:04:47.838 --> 00:04:49.336
But I think you might like this one.

00:04:49.642 --> 00:04:51.084
Okay, I’ll take this one.

00:04:51.405 --> 00:04:54.588
They’re so cute. I’ll wear them every day.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:56.731
- It really is adorable.
- Thank you.

00:04:56.811 --> 00:04:57.637
It’s my pleasure.

00:04:58.706 --> 00:04:59.814
What a cutie!

00:04:59.825 --> 00:05:00.634
Is my head gonna hit?

00:05:00.653 --> 00:05:01.825
No, but be careful.

00:05:05.256 --> 00:05:06.392
Can you hear my voice?

00:05:06.392 --> 00:05:07.263
[SEEMS LIKE SHE DOESN’T.]

00:05:07.263 --> 00:05:08.290
Can you hear me?
[SEEMS LIKE SHE DOESN’T.]

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:09.602
Of course, you can.

00:05:10.816 --> 00:05:11.976
Don’t pretend you can’t.
[OH! MY ACTING ISN’T GOOD ENOUGH?]

00:05:11.976 --> 00:05:12.650
[OH! MY ACTING ISN’T GOOD ENOUGH?]

00:05:12.871 --> 00:05:14.016
Hey, there’s a mirror inside!

00:05:14.176 --> 00:05:16.438
There are holes here—
that’s why I can hear you.

00:05:16.531 --> 00:05:17.040
Hello!

00:05:17.054 --> 00:05:18.262
Bonnie, can you see me behind you?

00:05:19.499 --> 00:05:19.965
Hey.

00:05:21.007 --> 00:05:22.063
Hello!

00:05:23.687 --> 00:05:24.607
Is it about time to get out?

00:05:24.945 --> 00:05:25.469
Nope.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.534
And here’s our food!

00:05:33.551 --> 00:05:34.770
We’ve got black tea and flower tea.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.382
I actually wanted the flower tea,

00:05:36.397 --> 00:05:38.900
but P’Emi wanted it, so I made a sacrifice.

00:05:38.992 --> 00:05:40.069
You’re making me look bad.
[GIRL, YOU ORDERED IT YOURSELF.]

00:05:40.069 --> 00:05:41.240
[GIRL, YOU ORDERED IT YOURSELF.]

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.360
You were the one placing the orders!
[GIRL, YOU ORDERED IT YOURSELF.]

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:42.385
[GIRL, YOU ORDERED IT YOURSELF.]

00:05:42.385 --> 00:05:42.730
We can share.
[GIRL, YOU ORDERED IT YOURSELF.]

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:43.448
We can share.

00:05:43.478 --> 00:05:44.367
Okay, sure.

00:05:46.543 --> 00:05:48.376
Mmm. Good.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.370
Just the kind of taste I like.
[WHAT A DRAMATIC REACTION!]

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:53.797
It has a nice scent, and…

00:05:54.265 --> 00:05:54.908
It’s not too sweet.

00:05:54.971 --> 00:05:55.810
That’s right.

00:05:55.896 --> 00:05:57.767
(There’s a game for you two.)

00:05:57.807 --> 00:05:59.354
(Stare into each other’s eyes.)

00:05:59.367 --> 00:06:00.628
Oh, this is my area of expertise.

00:06:01.155 --> 00:06:03.703
(Wehover blinks or looks away first loses.
There’s a punishment too.)

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:04.739
What’s the punishment?

00:06:04.783 --> 00:06:05.549
We don’t get to know first?

00:06:05.558 --> 00:06:06.247
(Nope.)

00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:07.432
(Are you ready?)

00:06:07.757 --> 00:06:09.031
I’m gonna lose.

00:06:09.192 --> 00:06:10.232
What’s wrong? Is it your eyelashes?

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:11.300
I’m wearing contacts today.
[THAT INTENSE STARE.]

00:06:11.308 --> 00:06:12.251
You’re not, are you?
[THAT INTENSE STARE.]

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:13.377
Why are you looking at me like that…
[THAT INTENSE STARE.]

00:06:13.397 --> 00:06:14.069
I’m ready.

00:06:14.105 --> 00:06:14.762
(Okay, ready?)

00:06:14.782 --> 00:06:15.808
I can’t hold back my laugh.

00:06:15.872 --> 00:06:19.438
(Five, four, three… go!)

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:27.930
[BOTH ARE HOLDING STRONG.]

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:34.444
[EVEN A BLOW WON’T BREAK HER.]

00:06:34.444 --> 00:06:34.982
Hey!
[EVEN A BLOW WON’T BREAK HER.]

00:06:34.982 --> 00:06:35.650
[EVEN A BLOW WON’T BREAK HER.]

00:06:35.786 --> 00:06:37.717
You’re wearing contacts.

00:06:37.928 --> 00:06:39.525
Yeah, and they make my eyes even drier.

00:06:39.525 --> 00:06:40.688
[BONNIE FINALLY BLINKS!]

00:06:40.688 --> 00:06:42.050
Ugh, my eyes are so sore now.
[BONNIE FINALLY BLINKS!]

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:43.546
(Bonnie lost.)

00:06:44.419 --> 00:06:46.641
Guys, I lost.

00:06:46.985 --> 00:06:48.280
(The punishment is pretty easy.)

00:06:48.297 --> 00:06:49.077
What is it?

00:06:49.094 --> 00:06:50.282
(Go live on Instagram. Right now.)

00:06:50.302 --> 00:06:51.091
Seriously?

00:06:51.161 --> 00:06:51.988
(Stay live for ten minutes.)

00:06:52.952 --> 00:06:53.592
Seriously?

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:56.954
(Oh, and for the entire 10 minutes,
you have to keep talking nonstop.)

00:06:56.957 --> 00:06:58.250
[SOMEONE LOOKS WAY TOO HAPPY ABOUT THIS.]

00:06:58.428 --> 00:06:59.983
Who has to talk nonstop? Both of us?

00:07:00.044 --> 00:07:00.721
Nope. Just you, Bonnie.

00:07:01.717 --> 00:07:02.699
I won the game.

00:07:02.899 --> 00:07:03.382
Let’s start.

00:07:03.401 --> 00:07:06.131
Three, two, one.

00:07:06.397 --> 00:07:07.431
Hey, we’re live!

00:07:07.482 --> 00:07:08.565
Hi, everyone.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:09.896
- No one’s watching yet.
- 	Oh.

00:07:09.934 --> 00:07:11.108
Anyone here yet?

00:07:11.306 --> 00:07:12.278
(Bonnie, you can’t stop talking.)

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:13.721
Bla bla bla…

00:07:13.721 --> 00:07:15.010
[GOING BONKERS IS THE BEST STRATEGY.]

00:07:15.143 --> 00:07:15.893
You can’t stop,

00:07:15.906 --> 00:07:17.174
so just talk about food or something.

00:07:17.186 --> 00:07:20.444
Okay, today we’re reviewing tea!

00:07:20.684 --> 00:07:24.610
Let’s start with this flower tea.

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:26.949
- Hi, guys.
- Wow, it’s so good.

00:07:27.074 --> 00:07:28.357
Wait, we have 2,000 viewers now, Bonnie.

00:07:28.382 --> 00:07:29.797
I’m nervous now. I’m an introvert.

00:07:29.835 --> 00:07:30.520
Yeah, nervous.

00:07:30.805 --> 00:07:32.468
Where are we right now, Bonnie? Tell them.

00:07:32.499 --> 00:07:35.096
We’re at P’Pam’s house.

00:07:36.808 --> 00:07:37.795
Looks like it.

00:07:37.903 --> 00:07:38.665
Yeah?

00:07:38.682 --> 00:07:39.640
It does.

00:07:39.801 --> 00:07:42.730
I’m being punished with this livestream.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:44.379
I have to talk nonstop.

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:45.847
Bonnie lost the game.

00:07:45.994 --> 00:07:47.328
I lose every game.

00:07:47.717 --> 00:07:48.702
Have I ever won?

00:07:48.878 --> 00:07:50.494
“You need anti-losing pills.”

00:07:51.444 --> 00:07:52.540
Yeah, I lose all the time.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.254
Hi, everyone.

00:07:54.333 --> 00:07:55.392
P’Emi, why don’t you help me talk?

00:07:55.417 --> 00:07:57.960
I can’t really see. I’m shortsighted.

00:07:58.117 --> 00:07:59.398
(Talk about episode five of your series.)

00:08:00.253 --> 00:08:01.989
The opening scene of episode five is so sad.

00:08:02.198 --> 00:08:03.260
But it turns happy pretty quickly.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:06.202
Still, it made me sad.
I was sad after watching it.

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:07.225
How do I eat this?

00:08:07.531 --> 00:08:07.982
Just bite it.

00:08:08.002 --> 00:08:09.395
Let me set up the camera.

00:08:12.591 --> 00:08:13.801
Is it better than what I made?

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:17.665
Your silence says it all.

00:08:17.912 --> 00:08:19.394
Food made by P’Emi is the best.

00:08:20.242 --> 00:08:21.688
Guys, this is so good.

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:23.094
Yum.

00:08:24.653 --> 00:08:25.220
Yum.

00:08:26.099 --> 00:08:26.872
So good.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:27.794
Try it.

00:08:27.881 --> 00:08:28.720
It’s not too mushy.

00:08:33.376 --> 00:08:36.053
Give us your review. You want to be
a food reviewer, right?

00:08:36.066 --> 00:08:37.545
- Is this food or dessert?
- It’s dessert.

00:08:37.844 --> 00:08:39.250
- It’s blueberry.
- What’s giving it that sour, savory taste?

00:08:42.401 --> 00:08:44.917
What do you mean by ‘savory and sour’?

00:08:45.422 --> 00:08:46.419
You’re taking a lot of bites.

00:08:46.441 --> 00:08:47.768
- It’s good.
- You’re really taking a lot of bites.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:48.660
Are you being stingy?

00:08:50.106 --> 00:08:51.060
What do you mean?

00:08:51.376 --> 00:08:54.619
- We should do a food live at midnight.
- Yes.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.296
I used to go live at 3 AM.

00:08:56.428 --> 00:08:56.868
Why?

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.411
I did ASMR, eating Mala.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:08:59.277
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:08:59.312 --> 00:09:02.425
Whoever watched P’Emi’s live on TikTok at 3 AM…

00:09:02.438 --> 00:09:04.717
Wait! Not Mala, it’s marinated salmon.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:05.711
You eat salmon?
[SHE SAID SHE DOESN’T EAT RAW SALMON.]

00:09:05.714 --> 00:09:06.758
- You said you didn’t eat salmon.
- It’s marinated.
[SHE SAID SHE DOESN’T EAT RAW SALMON.]

00:09:06.774 --> 00:09:07.800
Isn’t marinated salmon raw?

00:09:08.226 --> 00:09:08.991
Yeah, it is, but…
[IT’S RAW!]

00:09:08.991 --> 00:09:09.290
[IT’S RAW!]

00:09:10.869 --> 00:09:12.626
Like I said, I like seafood sauce.

00:09:12.718 --> 00:09:16.595
We always eat it with
seafood sauce and seaweed wrap.

00:09:16.914 --> 00:09:18.789
I’ll eat marinated salmon

00:09:18.802 --> 00:09:20.648
as long as it’s with
seafood sauce and seaweed wrap.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:21.675
So do you like raw salmon or not?

00:09:21.687 --> 00:09:22.265
No.

00:09:23.005 --> 00:09:24.506
You all heard that, right?

00:09:24.949 --> 00:09:26.997
It’s almost time—we have to go soon.

00:09:27.103 --> 00:09:28.635
Yeah, we’re in a bit of a rush.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:29.725
Oh, I forgot to show you this.

00:09:31.312 --> 00:09:33.321
Look. Is her necklace cute?

00:09:33.391 --> 00:09:34.549
I just got it today.

00:09:34.555 --> 00:09:37.469
It changes color based on the ‘hotness’
of the person wearing it.

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:39.305
But the auntie said,

00:09:39.321 --> 00:09:41.200
“Oh, it’s not changing.
Maybe you’re not hot enough.”

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:43.010
[DON’T TEASE HER.]

00:09:43.121 --> 00:09:44.037
“Why isn’t it changing?”

00:09:44.048 --> 00:09:45.845
“Because you’re not hot, you’re cute.”

00:09:46.219 --> 00:09:47.219
- Yeah?
- That’s what she said.

00:09:47.232 --> 00:09:48.954
She called you cute.

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:50.130
What if you wear it?

00:09:50.262 --> 00:09:51.118
It’ll turn red.

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:52.850
[TOO HOT TO HANDLE.]

00:09:52.974 --> 00:09:54.425
But it’s beautiful.

00:09:54.454 --> 00:09:56.082
- I’ll try putting it in the fridge.
- I also got this one.

00:09:56.151 --> 00:09:57.949
That’s right. It’s a butterfly.

00:09:58.164 --> 00:10:01.413
All right, guys, time for us to go.

00:10:01.428 --> 00:10:02.285
That’s right.

00:10:02.573 --> 00:10:06.490
- If you miss us, you can watch our series.
- Don’t forget to watch episode five.

00:10:06.678 --> 00:10:08.428
Alright, goodbye to my 2 billion viewers.

00:10:08.444 --> 00:10:09.610
See you next time!

00:10:10.225 --> 00:10:11.096
It’s your turn to open it.

00:10:11.211 --> 00:10:12.346
Place of Us.

00:10:12.546 --> 00:10:15.029
I’m opening it since Bonnie’s hands are occupied.

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:17.721
Next stop—Taihua Shrine.

00:10:17.875 --> 00:10:19.211
What’s this shrine known for?

00:10:19.256 --> 00:10:20.063
This.

00:10:20.733 --> 00:10:21.518
Lotus?

00:10:22.672 --> 00:10:23.460
For granting love wishes?

00:10:23.555 --> 00:10:24.325
For love.

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:26.672
Right. I’m going to pray.

00:10:26.745 --> 00:10:28.551
We’re still in the café.
[YOU HAVEN’T EVEN MOVED YET.]

00:10:28.551 --> 00:10:28.976
[YOU HAVEN’T EVEN MOVED YET.]

00:10:28.976 --> 00:10:30.450
We’re not at the shrine. You’re already praying.
[YOU HAVEN’T EVEN MOVED YET.]

00:10:30.517 --> 00:10:31.077
Let’s go.

00:10:31.337 --> 00:10:31.875
Yeah, let’s move.

00:10:32.094 --> 00:10:32.709
Can you read the map?

00:10:32.737 --> 00:10:34.014
I’m not great with walkways,

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:35.637
but if it’s a map for driving, I’m pretty good.

00:10:35.696 --> 00:10:36.642
Which way should we go?
[LOOKS LIKE THEY’RE LOST AGAIN.]

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:37.274
This way.
[LOOKS LIKE THEY’RE LOST AGAIN.]

00:10:37.274 --> 00:10:37.284
[LOOKS LIKE THEY’RE LOST AGAIN.]

00:10:37.284 --> 00:10:38.164
This way?
[LOOKS LIKE THEY’RE LOST AGAIN.]

00:10:38.164 --> 00:10:38.210
[LOOKS LIKE THEY’RE LOST AGAIN.]

00:10:41.521 --> 00:10:43.771
Okay, six minutes to go.

00:10:43.903 --> 00:10:45.841
You know, this vlog is just

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:47.994
a sneaky way to make us walk and lose weight.

00:10:47.994 --> 00:10:48.930
[A FULL EPISODE OF WALKING.]

00:11:06.982 --> 00:11:07.937
Should we go straight?

00:11:08.165 --> 00:11:10.022
Come on, we’re almost there.

00:11:10.198 --> 00:11:11.317
And…

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:12.108
here we are.

00:11:12.256 --> 00:11:13.482
We made it!

00:11:13.885 --> 00:11:14.942
Wow, this place is huge.

00:11:15.102 --> 00:11:17.324
The child in your womb will be female.

00:11:18.874 --> 00:11:19.514
When?

00:11:19.844 --> 00:11:21.136
They’re kissing.

00:11:21.312 --> 00:11:22.551
Do we have to follow the reference?

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:23.238
We don’t have to.

00:11:23.259 --> 00:11:24.640
Ah!

00:11:24.874 --> 00:11:26.201
You can’t be here. Look.

00:11:26.647 --> 00:11:27.564
“Don’t strike a pose.”

00:11:27.754 --> 00:11:28.642
I can’t be here.

00:11:28.921 --> 00:11:29.548
It’s good.

00:11:29.597 --> 00:11:30.044
It is.

00:11:30.066 --> 00:11:31.764
I don’t get to do things like this very much.

00:11:32.404 --> 00:11:33.158
Thank you.

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:34.374
(Don’t cry.)

00:11:35.311 --> 00:11:36.205
Are you about to cry?

